  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * @brief  Adds a constant offset to a Q7 vector.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * @param[in]  *pSrc points to the input vector
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * @param[in]  offset is the offset to be added
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * @param[out]  *pDst points to the output vector
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * @param[in]  blockSize number of samples in the vector
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * @return none.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  *
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * \par
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * The function uses saturating arithmetic.
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  * Results outside of the allowable Q7 range [0x80 0x7F] are saturated.
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c ****  */
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_offset_q7.c **** 
